Server functions can be configured to validate their input data at runtime, while adding type safety.
This is useful for ensuring the input is of the correct type before executing the server function, and providing more friendly error messages.
This is done with the validator method.
It will accept whatever input is passed to the server function.
The value (and type) you return from this function will become the input passed to the actual server function handler.
